course: dictionary
lesson: 8833
title: Shingle: stones, roofs or illness?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shingle most often means small round stones on a beach. They are bigger than sand. «A spit is a long finger of sand or shingle stretching out from the coast into the sea.» Sand is very fine, so the word next to it tells you that shingle means bigger pieces.
explain: The same spelling can mean other things. On a roof, shingles are thin flat pieces of wood or another material, laid in overlapping rows. In a story, «the Mariner walks out onto the "shingle" (a beach of small pebbles)» and the words in brackets show you the meaning.
explain: Shingles is different again. It is an illness, with no singular form, and it is caused by the same virus as chickenpox. «After chickenpox you are usually immune, but the virus sleeps in the nerves and can wake years later as shingles, a painful rash.» Look for clues such as rash and virus to tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Shingle means small round stones on a beach, larger than sand.
fact: Shingle can also mean a thin flat piece of wood or other material laid in overlapping rows on a roof or wall.
fact: Shingles is an illness that causes a painful rash, and it is caused by the same virus as chickenpox.
fact: «Hang out your shingle» means to start your own business, and it is mostly used in the United States.
fact: Chesil Beach in England is a shingle beach, shaped by waves.
exercise: «A spit is a long finger of sand or shingle stretching out from the coast into the sea.» What is shingle here? | A painful rash | *Small round stones on a beach | A sign outside a doctor's office | A thin wooden tile for a roof
exercise: «The virus sleeps in the nerves and can wake years later as shingles, a painful rash.» What is shingles in this sentence? | Small round stones on a beach | A kind of sea fish | Thin flat tiles laid on a roof | *An illness with a painful rash, caused by the same virus as chickenpox
exercise: Which meaning of shingle fits a roof? | *A thin flat piece of wood laid in overlapping rows | A beach of sand | A long finger of land | Small round pebbles
test: «The Mariner walks out onto the "shingle" (a beach of small pebbles).» Where is the Mariner walking? | A kitchen floor | *A beach of small pebbles | A field of long grass | A railway platform
test: In the US, «hang out your shingle» means what? | Put washing outside to dry | Visit the doctor | Put up a beach sign | *Start your own business
exam: Which word names an illness caused by the same virus as chickenpox? | *shingles | shingle | nerve | immune
